      "writtenOn": "2023-07-31T18:51:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure how much it matters, but the behavior of this is a little different from before. It used to map ifindex -\u003e ifname, so if an ifindex was reused by another interface (through a sequence of adding/removing interfaces), it would _only_ map to the new interface name. With the way this cache is updated, multiple ifnames can map to the same ifindex, potentially double counting traffic depending on how this is used.\n\n@maze: even the old system seems tenuous at best. Any suggestions?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "ffa1adfaaf31231d5124bcaed88639116c54592e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fddccb1b_7c293fa4",
        "filename": "service-t/src/com/android/server/net/BpfInterfaceMapUpdater.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003247
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-31T19:07:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ifindex reuse should theoretically not happen.\n\nnewly created interfaces in the root netns get increasing ifindexes...\n\nI guess it could be done via interface renames, but that should basically not happen... I\u0027m sure something else somewhere else would break...\n\n--\n\nmaybe we should make sure to remove ifindex from any other map it might have previously been in? just to be safe?",
      "parentUuid": "cea39d85_9e75d1ef",
